SERVICE LIFECYCLE AND UPDATES
-----------------------------
DXSpider, DXWeb and DXWeb Admin are three separate services. DXWeb and
DXWeb Admin can each be started, stopped, enabled or disabled independently
of the DXSpider service. However, their live DXSpider-backed functionality
requires a running and reachable DXSpider IntMsg listener.

A DXSpider source update does not automatically reload code in already
running processes. If an update changes DXWeb or DXWeb Admin files, restart
the corresponding web service(s) to load those changes. Changes to Perl
modules loaded by DXSpider (such as perl/Web.pm) require a DXSpider restart;
restarting only the web services will not load them.

For a coordinated restart after a DXSpider update, when operationally
acceptable and after arranging for the brief service interruption:

  systemctl restart dxspider.service
  systemctl restart dxweb.service dxweb-admin.service

Check service status afterward:

  systemctl status dxspider.service dxweb.service dxweb-admin.service --no-pager

Restarting all three is recommended after an update affecting multiple
components, but is not required for a web-only update. Use the actual
installed service names if they differ. Restarting DXSpider interrupts
active DX cluster connections and should be scheduled accordingly.


